    question: "What is the Virtual DOM and how does it work?",
    idealAnswer: "**Virtual DOM** is a JavaScript representation of the real DOM. It's a lightweight copy that React uses to optimize UI updates.\n\n**How it Works:**\n1. React creates a virtual DOM tree\n2. When state changes, React creates a new virtual DOM tree\n3. React compares the new tree with the old tree (diffing)\n4. React calculates the minimum changes needed\n5. React updates only the changed parts in the real DOM\n\n**Benefits:**\n- **Performance**: Fewer DOM manipulations\n- **Batch updates**: Multiple changes are applied together\n- **Declarative**: Describe what you want, not how to update\n\n**Example:**\n```jsx\n// Virtual DOM representation\nconst virtualElement = {\n  type: 'div',\n  props: { className: 'container' },\n  children: [\n    { type: 'h1', props: {}, children: ['Hello'] },\n    { type: 'p', props: {}, children: ['World'] }\n  ]\n};\n```"
