    question: "What is the difference between useMemo and useCallback?",
    idealAnswer: "**useMemo** and **useCallback** are hooks for optimizing performance by memoizing values and functions.\n\n**useMemo:**\n- Memoizes computed values\n- Returns the memoized value\n- Re-computes only when dependencies change\n\n```jsx\nfunction ExpensiveComponent({ items, filter }) {\n  const filteredItems = useMemo(() => {\n    console.log('Filtering items...');\n    return items.filter(item => \n      item.name.toLowerCase().includes(filter.toLowerCase())\n    );\n  }, [items, filter]); // Only re-computes when items or filter change\n  \n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {filteredItems.map(item => (\n        <li key={item.id}>{item.name}</li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**useCallback:**\n- Memoizes functions\n- Returns the memoized function\n- Recreates function only when dependencies change\n\n```jsx\nfunction ParentComponent() {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);\n  \n  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {\n    setCount(c => c + 1);\n  }, []); // Function reference never changes\n  \n  return <MemoizedChild onClick={handleClick} />;\n}\n\nconst MemoizedChild = React.memo(function Child({ onClick }) {\n  console.log('Child rendered');\n  return <button onClick={onClick}>Click me</button>;\n});\n```\n\n**Key Differences:**\n\n| Feature | useMemo | useCallback |\n|---------|---------|-------------|\n| Returns | Memoized value | Memoized function |\n| Use case | Expensive calculations | Stable function references |\n| Syntax | useMemo(() => compute, deps) | useCallback(() => fn, deps) |\n\n**Relationship:**\n```jsx\n// useCallback is essentially useMemo for functions\nconst memoizedCallback = useCallback(() => {\n  doSomething(a, b);\n}, [a, b]);\n\n// Equivalent to:\nconst memoizedCallback = useMemo(() => () => {\n  doSomething(a, b);\n}, [a, b]);\n```\n\n**When to Use Each:**\n\n**useMemo:**\n- Expensive calculations (filtering, sorting, data processing)\n- Derived state from props/state\n- Object creation to prevent reference changes\n\n**useCallback:**\n- Event handlers passed to memoized children\n- Functions used in useEffect dependencies\n- API calls with stable references"
