    question: "What are React Portals?",
    idealAnswer: "**React Portals** provide a way to render children into a DOM node that exists outside the hierarchy of the parent component.\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n```jsx\nimport { createPortal } from 'react-dom';\n\nfunction Modal({ children }) {\n  return createPortal(\n    <div className=\"modal-overlay\">\n      <div className=\"modal\">\n        {children}\n      </div>\n    </div>,\n    document.getElementById('modal-root')\n  );\n}\n\n// In your HTML\n<div id=\"root\"></div>\n<div id=\"modal-root\"></div>\n```\n\n**Use Cases:**\n\n**1. Modals and Dialogs:**\n```jsx\nfunction App() {\n  const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(false);\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={() => setShowModal(true)}>\n        Open Modal\n      </button>\n      \n      {showModal && (\n        <Modal>\n          <h2>Modal Title</h2>\n          <p>Modal content</p>\n          <button onClick={() => setShowModal(false)}>\n            Close\n          </button>\n        </Modal>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**2. Tooltips and Popovers:**\n```jsx\nfunction Tooltip({ children, text }) {\n  const [visible, setVisible] = useState(false);\n  \n  return (\n    <>\n      <div \n        onMouseEnter={() => setVisible(true)}\n        onMouseLeave={() => setVisible(false)}\n      >\n        {children}\n      </div>\n      \n      {visible && createPortal(\n        <div className=\"tooltip\">\n          {text}\n        </div>,\n        document.body\n      )}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**3. Notifications:**\n```jsx\nfunction Notification({ message, type }) {\n  return createPortal(\n    <div className={`notification notification-${type}`}>\n      {message}\n    </div>,\n    document.getElementById('notification-root')\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Event Bubbling:**\n```jsx\nfunction Modal({ onClose, children }) {\n  const handleClick = (e) => {\n    if (e.target === e.currentTarget) {\n      onClose();\n    }\n  };\n  \n  return createPortal(\n    <div className=\"modal-overlay\" onClick={handleClick}>\n      <div className=\"modal\" onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}>\n        {children}\n      </div>\n    </div>,\n    document.getElementById('modal-root')\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Break out of parent container limitations\n- Better CSS styling (z-index, positioning)\n- Accessibility improvements\n- Cleaner component structure\n\n**Considerations:**\n- Portals update React tree despite DOM location\n- Event bubbling works through portals\n- Need additional DOM nodes in HTML"
