    idealAnswer: "**Concurrent Mode** is a set of new features that help React apps stay responsive and gracefully adjust to the user's device capabilities and network speed.\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n**1. Interruptible Rendering**\n- React can pause and resume rendering work\n- More urgent updates can interrupt less urgent ones\n- Better user experience on slower devices\n\n**2. Time Slicing**\n- React breaks work into small chunks\n- Yields control back to browser periodically\n- Prevents blocking the main thread\n\n**3. Priority-Based Updates**\n```jsx\nimport { startTransition } from 'react';\n\nfunction SearchResults({ query }) {\n  const [results, setResults] = useState([]);\n  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState(query);\n  \n  const handleChange = (e) => {\n    setInputValue(e.target.value); // Urgent update\n    \n    startTransition(() => {\n      // Non-urgent update (can be interrupted)\n      setResults(searchResults(e.target.value));\n    });\n  };\n  \n  return (\n    <div>\n      <input value={inputValue} onChange={handleChange} />\n      <ResultsList results={results} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits:**\n- **Better user experience**: Apps stay responsive\n- **Smoother animations**: No janky updates\n- **Intelligent prioritization**: Important updates first\n- **Graceful degradation**: Works on slower devices"
