    question: "What is the difference between useEffect and useLayoutEffect?",
    idealAnswer: "**useEffect** and **useLayoutEffect** are both hooks for handling side effects, but they run at different times in the React render cycle.\n\n**Timing Differences:**\n```jsx\n// Render cycle order:\n// 1. Component renders\n// 2. useLayoutEffect runs (synchronous, before paint)\n// 3. Browser paints\n// 4. useEffect runs (asynchronous, after paint)\n```\n\n**useEffect:**\n```jsx\nimport { useEffect } from 'react';\n\nfunction Component() {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // Runs AFTER the component renders to the screen\n    console.log('Component has rendered');\n    \n    // Cleanup function\n    return () => {\n      console.log('Component will unmount or re-render');\n    };\n  }, [dependencies]);\n  \n  return <div>Content</div>;\n}\n```\n\n**useLayoutEffect:**\n```jsx\nimport { useLayoutEffect } from 'react';\n\nfunction Component() {\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    // Runs BEFORE the component paints to the screen\n    // Synchronous - blocks painting\n    console.log('Before paint');\n    \n    // Can read DOM layout here\n    const element = document.getElementById('my-element');\n    const rect = element.getBoundingClientRect();\n    \n    return () => {\n      console.log('Cleanup before re-render');\n    };\n  }, [dependencies]);\n  \n  return <div id=\"my-element\">Content</div>;\n}\n```\n\n**When to Use Each:**\n\n**useEffect for:**\n- Data fetching\n- Subscriptions\n- Side effects that don't affect layout\n- Most common use cases\n- Better performance (non-blocking)\n\n**useLayoutEffect for:**\n- DOM measurements\n- Layout calculations\n- Preventing visual flashes\n- Synchronous DOM mutations\n- When you need to read layout before paint"
